prompt_templates.omni_prompt_template:
The storyboard panel is the exact first frame of Shot 1 ({frame_file}). Do not freeze it: Shot 1 begins already in motion from that framing, with the same faces, wardrobe, props, location, light and color grade.

STORYBOARD PANEL (Shot 1 must match this exactly): {storyboard_panel}

IDENTITY ANCHORS (all present, fixed cast positions): {character_anchors}

{shot_block}

{timeline_block}

DIALOGUE (native audio, US English, lip-sync exact; maximum 15 words; finish before 8.5 s):
{dialogue_block}

AUDIO BED: {ambience}

CAMERA & MOVEMENT: {camera_block}

CONTINUITY: {continuity}

STYLE: {style}

RULES:
- Between 1 and 4 shots: follow the SHOT PLAN and TIMELINE exactly; every boundary listed is a hard cut at that second.
- One line, one shot: whoever speaks is on camera with face and mouth visible for the whole line, looking at the recipient; characters listed as silent in the shot plan keep their mouths closed.
- Silent shots (inserts, reactions, object details) carry no dialogue and never describe speaking.
- The story object from the shot plan stays visible on camera exactly as described; never show the inside of a bag, safe or container.
- Shot 1 starts in motion from the storyboard panel; never open on a static frame.
- Never insert the character reference sheet between scenes.
- One continuous 10-second take; never cut to a different location.
- Speak only the dialogue above. No narrator, no added voices, no subtitles or captions.
- No music, no score, no added sound design beyond the ambience and diegetic SFX listed.
- Keep faces stable and hands anatomically correct; no extra people.
- Native US English, conversational pace.

NEGATIVE: {negative}

DURATION: exactly 10.0 seconds. Aspect ratio 16:9.

